{
  "an5.162:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.162 ",
  "an5.162:0.2": "17. Resentment ",
  "an5.162:0.3": "Getting Rid of Resentment (2nd) ",
  "an5.162:1.1": "There Venerable Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an5.162:1.2": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "an5.162:1.3": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "an5.162:1.4": "Sāriputta said this: ",
  "an5.162:2.1": "“Reverends, a mendicant should use these five ways to completely get rid of resentment when it has arisen toward anyone. ",
  "an5.162:2.2": "What five? ",
  "an5.162:2.3": "In the case of an individual whose behavior by way of body is impure, but whose behavior by way of speech is pure, ",
  "an5.162:2.4": "you should get rid of resentment for that kind of individual. ",
  "an5.162:2.5": "In the case of an individual whose behavior by way of speech is impure, but whose behavior by way of body is pure, … ",
  "an5.162:2.6": "",
  "an5.162:2.7": "In the case of an individual whose behavior by way of body and speech is impure, but who gets an openness and clarity of heart from time to time, … ",
  "an5.162:2.8": "",
  "an5.162:2.9": "In the case of an individual whose behavior by way of body and speech is impure, and who doesn’t get an openness and clarity of heart from time to time, … ",
  "an5.162:2.10": "",
  "an5.162:2.11": "In the case of an individual whose behavior by way of body and speech is pure, and who gets an openness and clarity of heart from time to time, ",
  "an5.162:2.12": "you should get rid of resentment for that kin